        "original_id": "b3a4636e-5d44-54c0-8273-3879b2cb5805",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: San Andrés Accords\n- Organizations: Zapatista Army of National Liberation, Mexican government, Institutional Revolutionary Party\n- People: Ernesto Zedillo, Luis Téllez, Felipe Calderón\n- Roles: President of Mexico, Secretary of Energy, Secretary of Communications and Transportation\n\nFacts:\n- Ernesto Zedillo served as President of Mexico from December 1, 1994 to November 30, 2000.\n- Ernesto Zedillo was the last in the uninterrupted 70-year line of Mexican presidents from the Institutional Revolutionary Party.\n- The San Andrés Accords were agreements reached between the Zapatista Army of National Liberation and the Mexican government when Ernesto Zedillo headed the government.\n- Luis Téllez served as Secretary of Energy in the cabinet of Ernesto Zedillo.\n- Luis Téllez served as Secretary of Communications and Transportation in the cabinet of President Felipe Calderón until 2009.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
